.SH NAME
ssoossh-nss-config-check - Check nss.yaml, the override file and the fleet key without starting the daemon.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh-nss config check [flags] [args]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads what the daemon reads before it opens anything, through the same code: nss.yaml (--config), the host override file (--overrides) and the fleet key file nss.yaml names, with the same mode and owner checks (no group or other access to nss.yaml and the key, no group or other write to the override file, and, when run as root, owned by root). It reports every problem rather than the first, then the warnings a start logs, including the nsswitch.conf check.

.PP
Nothing is contacted: not the server, the running daemon or the cache. The key's secret is read but never printed. Run it as root, as the daemon runs, for the owner checks to apply.

.PP
Exit status: 0 when the daemon would start, warnings included; 1 when it would refuse to, or when the command itself fails.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for check

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the report as JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--admin-socket\fP="/run/ssoossh-nss/admin.sock"
	the admin socket the CLI and the daemon share

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss.yaml"
	the daemon's configuration file

.PP
\fB--overrides\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss-overrides.yaml"
	the host override file


